    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Has this difficulty with keeping things organized been a struggle for you throughout most of your life, or is this something that has only started happening more recently?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Um, well... I guess if I really think about it, it's... it's probably been around for a while. I hate to admit it, because I really don't want to sound like I'm just making excuses for myself, you know? But, um... yes, even way back in grade school, I guess it was a bit of a thing. \n\nMy teachers—they were always very kind about it, they told my mother I was a bright girl, which was sweet of them to say! But they did always mention that I was... well, \"scattered\" was the word they used a lot. I was always accidentally talking out of turn, or losing my school papers, and... they usually had to give me extra reminders to actually finish my work. \n\nI always just thought I was a bit too chatty, or maybe just not trying hard enough to be a good student. Is that... does that help answer your question? I hope I'm not oversharing or making a big deal out of normal kid stuff.",
