      "doctor_question": "Do you often feel like you have a constant need to be moving, or do you find it hard to sit still for long periods of time?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S011",
      "patient_response": "Um, well... I suppose I do have a little trouble with that sometimes. I mean, I don't want to make it sound like I'm bouncing off the walls or anything! I'm sure it's just a bit of restless energy, which is normal, right? \n\nBut, um... like, when I'm at church committee meetings, or when we have those fabric-care trainings at work... I do find myself getting up a lot. I always try to make it useful, you know? Like, I'll get up to grab a glass of water, or fetch some papers, or just go check on something really quick. It's just... I notice that everyone else seems perfectly fine just sitting there the whole time, and I'm the only one popping up and down. \n\nI try to be quiet about it so I don't bother anyone. I just... my legs get a little antsy if I sit for too long. Does that make sense? I hope that's the kind of thing you were asking about.",
